{"term":"manifest","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7d0c048a5047cfd4fd","definition":"Evident to the senses, especially to the sight; apparent; distinctly perceived.","example":"It re-envisioned Freddy Krueger in the “real world,” where the nightmare-dwelling being is made manifest in our reality, one where Freddy actor Robert Englund and original Nightmare On Elm Street star Heather Langenkamp play themselves, as does [Wes] Craven himself.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["apparent","plain","clear","distinct","obvious","palpable","patent"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["immanifest","manifest destiny","manifestly","manifestness","nonmanifest","premanifest","unmanifest"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manifest#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a5295a35e9253e0c3","definition":"Obvious to the understanding; apparent to the mind; easily apprehensible; plain; not obscure or hidden.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["immanifest","manifest destiny","manifestly","manifestness","nonmanifest","premanifest","unmanifest"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manifest#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:372fd1c17d973f9d26","definition":"Detect; convicted.","example":"Caliſtho there ſtood manifeſt of Shame, / And turn’d a Bear, the Northern Star became[…]","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"rare, with-of","register":"rare, with-of","wordFamily":["immanifest","manifest destiny","manifestly","manifestness","nonmanifest","premanifest","unmanifest"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manifest#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4